# One env var name per line, regenerated by its test. On 2026-10-18 it was the
# conflict in 12 of 18 conflicting PRs: two PRs each add a name at the same spot.
# `merge=union` keeps both sides' lines instead of conflicting. That is safe only
# because src/config/__tests__/env-read-names.test.ts fails unless the list is
# exactly the sorted names src/ reads (no missing, stale, duplicate or misordered
# line), and Unit Tests runs it on every PR and in the merge queue. If that check
# is ever loosened, remove this line. Fix a failure by regenerating:
#   UPDATE_ENV_READ_NAMES=1 pnpm vitest run src/config/__tests__/env-read-names.test.ts
# Recovery: merging a branch cut before #2019 (the old wrapped-paragraph format)
# exits 0 but leaves the file unparseable (old tail spliced after the new one). The
# test reads the file as text, so the same command still rewrites it; commit that.
# Hand-edited files (flag-manifest.ts, locale JSON) must never use union.
src/config/env-read-names.generated.ts merge=union
